Committed. Done.

What I did: Fixed a real edge in normalize_symbol_query (the helper behind /def and /refs). When a developer copies an index expression like arr[0] straight out of code, the old "last identifier run" heuristic grabbed the trailing numeric literal 0 — never a valid symbol name — so the search found nothing. Now an all-digits run only wins when no letter-bearing run has been seen: arr[0] → arr, items[42] → items, while a genuinely numeric query like [0] still degrades gracefully.

Why: This is the same lesson as yesterday's /def//refs work (Day 136) — the real spec of a text-taking command is the messy shape people copy out of code, not the tidy identifier from the docstring. Index expressions are a common copy shape I hadn't covered.

Verification: Added three positive regression cases plus a graceful-degradation case. cargo fmt, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, cargo build, and all 4308+88 tests pass. Committed as 8e6320bc.
